WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.903 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: WITH A
 FIRE AT ITS HEART...</i>

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.841 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE IS OUR
 FIRST NATIONAL PARK...</i>

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:13.380 line:0%
<i> A PRIMAL FORTRESS THAT
 SAVED THE DISAPPEARING WEST...</i>

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:19.419 line:0%
<i> THANKS TO ITS FIERCE WONDERS.</i>

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:24.557 line:0%
<i> MORE THAN THREE MILLION
VISITORS A YEAR COME TO MARVEL.</i>

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:28.794 line:0%
<i> BUT ONLY A HANDFUL
 VENTURE PAST THE LOOKOUTS.</i>

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:32.565 line:0%
<i> OVER THAT RIDGE AND INTO
 THE NEXT VALLEY IS WHERE</i>

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.802 line:0%
<i> THE REAL DRAMA HAPPENS.</i>

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.503 line:0%
<i> OLD BATTLES...</i>

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:38.938 line:0%
<i> NEW LIFE...</i>

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:42.508 line:0%
<i> AND UNEXPECTED COURAGE...</i>

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.045 line:0%
<i> IF YOU THINK YOU
 KNOW YELLOWSTONE...</i>

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.013 line:0%
<i> THINK AGAIN...</i>

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.585 line:0%
<i> YOU HAVE NEVER
 EXPERIENCED IT LIKE THIS.</i>

00:00:53.786 --> 00:01:00.527 line:0%
<i> ♪ [THEME MUSIC PLAYS] ♪</i>

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.802
♪ ♪

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.242 line:0%
<i> IN THE SHADOW OF THE ROCKIES,</i>

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.445 line:0%
<i> AN ANCIENT DRAMA
 IS ABOUT TO PLAY OUT....</i>

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:24.350 line:0%
<i> ONE THAT NEARLY DISAPPEARED
 FROM THE FACE OF THE EARTH:</i>

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:29.522 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE'S TOP PREDATOR
 AGAINST THE LARGEST MAMMAL</i>

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:34.194 line:0%
<i> IN NORTH AMERICA.</i>

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:39.365 line:0%
<i> ONCE ONLY 23
 BISON REMAINED HERE.</i>

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.834 line:0%
<i> AND NOT A SINGLE WOLF.</i>

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.837 line:0%
<i> BUT NOW THESE ETERNAL
 ENEMIES FACE OFF AGAIN...</i>

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:50.477 line:0%
<i> AS THEY DID LONG BEFORE
 ANY HUMAN SET FOOT HERE.</i>

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:59.686 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE HAS
 TURNED BACK TIME.</i>

00:02:02.087 --> 00:02:07.093 line:0%
<i> IT'S LATE WINTER IN
 AMERICA'S FIRST NATIONAL PARK,</i>

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:11.698 line:0%
<i> AND THE WORLD'S.</i>

00:02:14.666 --> 00:02:18.471 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE IS A MELTING POT
 OF SAVAGE BEAUTY CREATED BY</i>

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:23.843 line:0%
<i> ONE OF THE BIGGEST EXPLOSIONS
 EVER TO ROCK THE EARTH.</i>

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:29.816 line:0%
<i> AND ITS VIOLENT
 HEART STILL SMOLDERS...</i>

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:33.353 line:0%
<i> BLOWING OFF STEAM
 THROUGH SOME 300 GEYSERS...</i>

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:38.391 line:0%
<i> MORE THAN ANYWHERE
 ELSE IN THE WORLD.</i>

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.804 line:0%
<i> THE MOST FAMOUS GEYSER,
 OLD FAITHFUL,</i>

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:55.975 line:0%
<i> HURLS HOT WATER 150 FEET
 INTO THE AIR VENTING ITS RAGE</i>

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.911 line:0%
<i> EVERY 60 TO 90 MINUTES.</i>

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:01.747 line:0%
<i> THAT'S HOW LONG IT TAKES
 TO BUILD UP ENOUGH PRESSURE</i>

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:06.252 line:0%
<i> TO TURN GROUNDWATER
 INTO EXPLOSIVE STEAM.</i>

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:13.492 line:0%
<i> SOME BISON TAKE REFUGE IN
 THE STINKING SULFUROUS HEAT...</i>

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:18.598 line:0%
<i> A LAST HAVEN FOR
 THE WEAK AND WEARY.</i>

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.266 line:0%
<i> BUT ELSEWHERE IN THE PARK,</i>

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:26.406 line:0%
<i> THEY MUST FACE THE
 BRUTAL WINTER HEAD-ON.</i>

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.378 line:0%
<i> MOTHERS-TO-BE
 STRUGGLE TERRIBLY,</i>

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:37.750 line:0%
<i> TRYING TO FIND ENOUGH FOOD
FOR TWO IN THE RELENTLESS SNOW.</i>

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.853 line:0%
<i> THE CALF SHE CARRIES IS A
 REMINDER OF A MIRACULOUS</i>

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:45.057 line:0%
<i> COMEBACK, IF SHE CAN HOLD
 ON THROUGH YELLOWSTONE'S</i>

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:49.529 line:0%
<i> NOTORIOUSLY HARSH WINTER.</i>

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.867 line:0%
<i> BUT SPRING IS LATE THIS YEAR,</i>

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:58.704 line:0%
<i> TEMPERATURES HOVER WELL
BELOW FREEZING AND THE SNOWPACK</i>

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:02.008 line:0%
<i> DOES NOT GIVE WAY.</i>

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:05.444 line:0%
<i> THE GRAZING ANIMALS MUST
 STRUGGLE MIGHTILY IN SEARCH OF</i>

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.380 line:0%
<i> A FEW BLADES OF GRASS.</i>

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:12.484 line:0%
<i> MANY ELK GROW WEAK
 AS WINTER DRAGS ON...</i>

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.154 line:0%
<i> BUT SOMEONE ELSE GROWS STRONG.</i>

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.823 line:0%
<i> THE WOLF THRIVES IN WINTER.</i>

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.326 line:0%
<i> HIGHLY INTELLIGENT
 AND SOCIAL CREATURES,</i>

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:24.797 line:0%
<i> THEY OFTEN SHOW DEEP
 AFFECTION FOR ONE ANOTHER.</i>

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:27.433 line:0%
<i> THEIR INTENSE FAMILY
 TIES ALSO MAKE THEM A</i>

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.269 line:0%
<i> DEADLY HUNTING UNIT.</i>

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:33.106 line:0%
<i> ONCE COMPLETELY
 EXTERMINATED FROM THE PARK,</i>

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:36.475 line:0%
<i> GRAY WOLVES WERE
 REINTRODUCED IN 1995 AND</i>

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:40.279 line:0%
<i> HAVE BECOME A VITAL PLAYER
 IN THE PARK'S ECOSYSTEM.</i>

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.581 line:0%
<i> EAGERLY CHASING
 A BIG BULL ELK,</i>

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:47.687 line:0%
<i> THE WOLF IS IN ITS
 ELEMENT IN YELLOWSTONE.</i>

00:04:57.229 --> 00:05:03.970
♪ ♪

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:17.283
♪ ♪

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:24.324 line:0%
<i> BUT THIS BULL DIDN'T EARN HIS
 RACK BY BEING ANYONE'S FOOL.</i>

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.063 line:0%
<i> HE FINDS REFUGE IN
 THE FRIGID LAMAR RIVER,</i>

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:33.198 line:0%
<i> WHERE THE WOLVES
 CANNOT FOLLOW.</i>

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:38.137 line:0%
<i> AND AIMS HIS
 IMPRESSIVE RACK AT THEM.</i>

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:50.749 line:0%
<i> [HOWL]</i>

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:53.218 line:0%
<i> BUT ANOTHER DINNER AWAITS...</i>

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:57.423 line:0%
<i> AS THE REST OF
 THE PACK ANNOUNCES.</i>

00:05:57.823 --> 00:06:00.893 line:0%
<i> THEY'VE TAKEN A WEAKENED
 BISON DURING THE NIGHT AND</i>

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:04.130 line:0%
<i> THERE'S MORE THAN
 ENOUGH TO GO AROUND.</i>

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.132 line:0%
<i> WITH SUCH A
 LARGE PACK TO FEED,</i>

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:12.872 line:0%
<i> THEY NEED TO HUNT
 SUCCESSFULLY NEARLY EVERY DAY.</i>

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:20.078 line:0%
<i> BUT THE WINTER ITSELF IS
 FAR MORE DEADLY THAN WOLVES.</i>

00:06:20.178 --> 00:06:25.651 line:0%
<i> ONE OUT OF TEN BISON WILL
 DIE BEFORE THE SEASON IS DONE.</i>

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:30.389 line:0%
<i> FOR OUR MOTHER-TO-BE IT
 IS A PARTICULARLY HARD TIME.</i>

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:34.660 line:0%
<i> THE SCARCITY OF FOOD
 MEANS MANY ARE STARVING.</i>

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.863 line:0%
<i> WITH WEARY, MASSIVE HEADS,
 THEY PLOW THROUGH 4-FOOT</i>

00:06:37.963 --> 00:06:43.101 line:0%
<i> DRIFTS IN SEARCH
 OF ANYTHING EDIBLE.</i>

00:06:43.201 --> 00:06:47.740 line:0%
<i> THEY ARE THE LAST TRULY WILD
 BISON IN THE UNITED STATES.</i>

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.244 line:0%
<i> SOME 30 MILLION OF THEM ONCE
 BLANKETED THE AMERICAN PLAINS;</i>

00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:58.216 line:0%
<i> IT COULD TAKE SIX DAYS FOR
 A SINGLE HERD TO PASS YOU BY.</i>

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:02.321 line:0%
<i> BUT BY 1900, ONLY A
 HEARTBREAKING TWO DOZEN</i>

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:05.124 line:0%
<i> CLUNG TO LIFE IN THE
 CENTER OF THE PARK,</i>

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:10.863 line:0%
<i> THE LAST REFUGEES OF A
 CENTURY OF PERSECUTION.</i>

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.966 line:0%
<i> PROTECTED IN 1902,
 THEY'VE SLOWLY REBOUNDED TO</i>

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.836 line:0%
<i> ABOUT 5,000 TODAY.</i>

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:22.875 line:0%
<i> BUT IN A TERRIBLE WINTER,
 THEIR NUMBERS COULD CRASH.</i>

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.914 line:0%
<i> WITH THE BISON
 CARCASS PICKED CLEAN,</i>

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:31.150 line:0%
<i> THE LAMAR WOLF PACK'S
 SPECTACULAR ALPHA FEMALE IS ON</i>

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.854 line:0%
<i> THE LOOKOUT FOR MORE MEAT.</i>

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:40.092 line:0%
<i> AND AN ELK CALF HAS
 STRAYED FROM ITS HERD...</i>

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:49.034 line:0%
<i> WITH THE POWER AND CUNNING
 BORN OF LONG EXPERIENCE,</i>

00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:52.905 line:0%
<i> SHE'S LIKE A HEAT
 SEEKING MISSILE.</i>

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:08.654
♪ ♪

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:18.164 line:0%
<i> THIS IS A SLIPPERY SLOPE.</i>

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:33.980 line:0%
<i> [BIRDS CAWING]</i>

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:39.518 line:0%
<i> THE DEATH OF THE ELK CALF
 MEANS A REPRIEVE FOR</i>

00:08:39.618 --> 00:08:41.987 line:0%
<i> OUR PREGNANT BISON...</i>

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:45.658 line:0%
<i> BUT FOR HOW LONG?</i>

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:50.529 line:0%
<i> [HOWL]</i>

00:08:50.929 --> 00:08:54.666 line:0%
<i> IN WINTER, THE ALCHEMY OF
 HEAT BELOW AND COLD ABOVE</i>

00:08:54.766 --> 00:08:59.338 line:0%
<i> MAKES YELLOWSTONE LOOK
 LIKE A DIFFERENT PLANET.</i>

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:10.082 line:0%
<i> EVEN AT 50 DEGREES BELOW,
 THERE'S MAGIC IN THE AIR.</i>

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:20.893
♪ ♪

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:25.364 line:0%
<i> EXTREME SUB-ZERO TEMPERATURES
 IN A CLOUDLESS SKY SOMETIMES</i>

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:29.335 line:0%
<i> RESULT IN A
 FASCINATING PHENOMENON:</i>

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:35.274 line:0%
<i> THE FORMATION OF
 DELICATE ICE CRYSTALS...</i>

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:39.879 line:0%
<i> KNOWN AS "DIAMOND DUST".</i>

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:49.254 line:0%
<i> SOME BISON HAVE
 DEVISED A SPECIAL STRATEGY.</i>

00:09:49.354 --> 00:09:55.494 line:0%
<i> HOT SPRINGS GIVE OFF HEAT,
 ENABLING GRASS TO GROW.</i>

00:09:56.495 --> 00:10:02.668 line:0%
<i> A HASSLE-FREE SPA PACKAGE AT
 MINUS 20 DEGREES FAHRENHEIT.</i>

00:10:06.005 --> 00:10:07.873 line:0%
<i> WINTER IS IN SLOW RETREAT,</i>

00:10:07.973 --> 00:10:12.411 line:0%
<i> IN YELLOWSTONE'S
 OWN GRAND CANYON.</i>

00:10:12.511 --> 00:10:16.348 line:0%
<i> WARMER TEMPERATURES
UNLEASH THE FROZEN LOWER FALLS,</i>

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:21.253 line:0%
<i> TWICE THE HEIGHT OF NIAGARA.</i>

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:25.290 line:0%
<i> AND SOMEONE ELSE
 IS BEING UNLEASHED, TOO.</i>

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.725 line:0%
<i> JUST OUT OF HIBERNATION,</i>

00:10:26.825 --> 00:10:29.528 line:0%
<i> A YOUNG BEAR CAN'T
 RESIST THE AROMA...</i>

00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:32.898 line:0%
<i> OF FRESH CARRION.</i>

00:10:32.998 --> 00:10:35.334 line:0%
<i> A SECOND GRIZZLY
 HAS BEATEN HIM TO IT...</i>

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:37.603 line:0%
<i> THE CARCASS OF YET
 ANOTHER BISON THAT DIDN'T</i>

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:41.473 line:0%
<i> MAKE IT THROUGH THE WINTER.</i>

00:10:41.573 --> 00:10:44.476 line:0%
<i> AFTER SPENDING MORE THAN
 FOUR MONTHS IN THEIR DENS,</i>

00:10:44.576 --> 00:10:48.914 line:0%
<i> THEY'RE EAGER TO
 FIND SOME FOOD.</i>

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:54.186 line:0%
<i> BEARS LOSE UP TO A THIRD
 OF THEIR BODY WEIGHT</i>

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:56.388 line:0%
<i> DURING HIBERNATION.</i>

00:10:56.488 --> 00:10:58.257 line:0%
<i> AND THEY'RE RAVENOUS.</i>

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:02.194 line:0%
<i> SOMETHING'S GOTTA GIVE.</i>

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:06.999 line:0%
<i> GRIZZLIES WOULD RATHER
 INTIMIDATE THAN FIGHT;</i>

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:08.901 line:0%
<i> THERE'S JUST TOO
 MUCH RISK OF INJURY IN</i>

00:11:09.001 --> 00:11:13.205 line:0%
<i> BEAR-ON-BEAR VIOLENCE.</i>

00:11:17.943 --> 00:11:22.948 line:0%
<i> STANDING UP TO YOUR FULL
 HEIGHT IS MEANT TO IMPRESS...</i>

00:11:23.048 --> 00:11:26.752 line:0%
<i> OOPS.</i>

00:11:32.891 --> 00:11:35.528 line:0%
<i> THE OWNER OF THE
 CARCASS DECIDES TO SHOW HIM</i>

00:11:35.628 --> 00:11:39.531 line:0%
<i> HOW IT'S DONE.</i>

00:11:39.731 --> 00:11:41.967 line:0%
<i> BUT WHEN RITUALS FAIL...</i>

00:11:42.067 --> 00:11:45.438 line:0%
<i> VIOLENCE IS INEVITABLE.</i>

00:11:52.277 --> 00:11:57.149 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: HUNGRY
 BEARS ARE VIOLENT BEARS.</i>

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:07.893
♪ ♪

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:11.463 line:0%
<i> THE PAIR IS CLOSELY MATCHED
 AND EQUALLY DESPERATE FOR A</i>

00:12:11.563 --> 00:12:16.469 line:0%
<i> POST-HIBERNATION FEAST.</i>

00:12:26.211 --> 00:12:31.817 line:0%
<i> A FIGHT LIKE THIS IS A
 RARE SIGHT IN YELLOWSTONE.</i>

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:43.128 line:0%
<i> [GROWLING]</i>

00:12:43.229 --> 00:12:45.897 line:0%
<i> WITH A FINAL SLAP,
 THE NEWCOMER TELLS HIS</i>

00:12:45.997 --> 00:12:51.570 line:0%
<i> RIVAL TO "SHOVE OFF" AND
 CLAIMS HIS GRISLY PRIZE.</i>

00:12:56.908 --> 00:13:01.213 line:0%
<i> SPRING IS FINALLY
 HERE IN EARNEST.</i>

00:13:06.051 --> 00:13:12.190 line:0%
<i> IN THE VALLEYS, WARMER DAYS
 EASILY SHRUG OFF LATE SNOWS.</i>

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.260 line:0%
<i> IN THE PARK'S
 NORTH-EAST LIES SODA BUTTE,</i>

00:13:15.361 --> 00:13:20.666 line:0%
<i> A LIMESTONE MOUND
 CREATED BY A HOT SPRING.</i>

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:27.072 line:0%
<i> A MUDDY CONDO COMPLEX OF
 SORTS IS UNDER CONSTRUCTION.</i>

00:13:29.174 --> 00:13:32.110 line:0%
<i> AMERICAN CLIFF
 SWALLOWS ARE BUSY NESTING...</i>

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:37.283 line:0%
<i> THE MUD AT THE FOOT OF THE
 CONE MAKES A PERFECT CEMENT.</i>

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:49.995 line:0%
<i> BISON LOVE THE MUD
 OF SODA BUTTE TOO,</i>

00:13:50.095 --> 00:13:52.230 line:0%
<i> BECAUSE IT'S RICH
 WITH MINERALS....</i>

00:13:52.331 --> 00:13:57.002 line:0%
<i> MINERALS THAT THE
 PREGNANT FEMALES CRAVE.</i>

00:13:57.269 --> 00:13:59.605 line:0%
<i> SOON THE VALLEYS OF
 YELLOWSTONE WILL BE</i>

00:13:59.705 --> 00:14:03.242 line:0%
<i> FULL OF BABIES.</i>

00:14:03.342 --> 00:14:05.910 line:0%
<i> OUR MOTHER GROWS
 RESTLESS AND NERVOUS.</i>

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:09.281 line:0%
<i> WITH GOOD REASON.</i>

00:14:09.815 --> 00:14:11.316 line:0%
<i> DOWN THE VALLEY,</i>

00:14:11.416 --> 00:14:14.186 line:0%
<i> A PACK OF WOLVES HAS
 FOUND A STILLBORN CALF,</i>

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:16.722 line:0%
<i> BUT IT WILL ONLY
 FEED ONE OR TWO OF THEM.</i>

00:14:16.822 --> 00:14:20.526 line:0%
<i> SO THE REST HAVE
 TURNED ON THE MOTHER.</i>

00:14:23.328 --> 00:14:27.566 line:0%
<i> WEAK FROM HER ORDEAL,
 SHE IS TOUGH...</i>

00:14:28.033 --> 00:14:32.137 line:0%
<i> BUT VULNERABLE.</i>

00:14:40.178 --> 00:14:42.314 line:0%
<i> SHE MAKES A
 BREAK FOR THE HERD.</i>

00:14:42.414 --> 00:14:46.452 line:0%
<i> A RISKY DECISION.</i>

00:14:53.425 --> 00:14:55.527 line:0%
<i> EVEN WHEN SHE
 REACHES THE HERD,</i>

00:14:55.627 --> 00:14:58.764 line:0%
<i> THE WOLVES DON'T GIVE UP:
 BISON ARE MOST VULNERABLE TO</i>

00:14:58.864 --> 00:15:04.970 line:0%
<i> ATTACK FROM BEHIND...</i>

00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:14.045 line:0%
<i> FINALLY, THEY ROUND UP,
 CREATING A SHAGGY,</i>

00:15:14.145 --> 00:15:18.416 line:0%
<i> IMPENETRABLE FORTRESS.</i>

00:15:18.516 --> 00:15:24.590 line:0%
<i> ON THE SLOPES ABOVE, OUR
 HERD IS MISSING SOMEONE.</i>

00:15:26.324 --> 00:15:31.563 line:0%
<i> THE MOTHER HAS SLIPPED OFF
 INTO THE BRUSH TO GIVE BIRTH.</i>

00:15:32.864 --> 00:15:36.101 line:0%
<i> THIS MOVING AND INTIMATE
 MOMENT HAS RARELY BEEN SEEN</i>

00:15:36.201 --> 00:15:41.040 line:0%
<i> IN THE NATIONAL PARK.</i>

00:15:54.286 --> 00:16:00.526 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:14.673 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:16:14.773 --> 00:16:17.509 line:0%
<i> IMMEDIATELY THE LITTLE
 ONE STARTS SQUIRMING FREE</i>

00:16:17.609 --> 00:16:19.411 line:0%
<i> FROM THE AMNIOTIC SAC.</i>

00:16:19.511 --> 00:16:22.147 line:0%
<i> HE'S ONE OF ABOUT 700 BISON
 CALVES THAT WILL BE</i>

00:16:22.247 --> 00:16:27.219 line:0%
<i> BORN THIS YEAR.</i>

00:16:33.291 --> 00:16:35.961 line:0%
<i> THE MOTHER LOVINGLY
 CLEANS HER CALF,</i>

00:16:36.061 --> 00:16:37.462 line:0%
<i> URGING HIM TO HIS FEET...</i>

00:16:37.562 --> 00:16:39.665 line:0%
<i> HE'LL NEED TO BE ABLE
 TO RUN WITH THE HERD IN A</i>

00:16:39.765 --> 00:16:44.103 line:0%
<i> MATTER OF HOURS.</i>

00:16:53.679 --> 00:16:59.685
♪ ♪

00:17:03.555 --> 00:17:06.324 line:0%
<i> HE'S UP ON WOBBLY
 LEGS IN MINUTES....</i>

00:17:06.424 --> 00:17:11.063 line:0%
<i> ADORABLE AND OBLIVIOUS
 TO THE ASTOUNDING STRUGGLE</i>

00:17:11.163 --> 00:17:14.166 line:0%
<i> THAT LIES AHEAD.</i>

00:17:20.538 --> 00:17:22.206 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: IN THE
 HIGHER ELEVATIONS,</i>

00:17:22.307 --> 00:17:24.309 line:0%
<i> WHERE THE SNOW STILL HANGS ON,</i>

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:28.780 line:0%
<i> ANOTHER PREDATOR IS
 STAGING A COMEBACK.</i>

00:17:29.347 --> 00:17:32.050 line:0%
<i> IT'S THE NOTORIOUSLY
 SHY COUGAR,</i>

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.386 line:0%
<i> ONE OF ONLY
 ABOUT 20 IN THE PARK,</i>

00:17:34.486 --> 00:17:39.425 line:0%
<i> RETURNING TO HER ELK KILL.</i>

00:17:40.792 --> 00:17:44.229 line:0%
<i> THESE BIG CATS ARE SO
 ELUSIVE EVEN PARK RANGERS</i>

00:17:44.329 --> 00:17:46.264 line:0%
<i> RARELY SPOT THEM.</i>

00:17:46.364 --> 00:17:48.266 line:0%
<i> AT ONE POINT THEY
 WERE VIRTUALLY ELIMINATED</i>

00:17:48.366 --> 00:17:52.337 line:0%
<i> FROM YELLOWSTONE.</i>

00:17:53.939 --> 00:17:58.676 line:0%
<i> THE RAVEN SHOULD BE
 CAREFUL ABOUT COMPLAINING.</i>

00:17:59.277 --> 00:18:04.216 line:0%
<i> COUGARS CAN LEAP
 15 FEET STRAIGHT UP.</i>

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.323 line:0%
<i> SHE'S NOT ALONE.</i>

00:18:14.893 --> 00:18:17.929 line:0%
<i> HER THREE-MONTH-OLD
 KITTEN IS STILL NURSING BUT</i>

00:18:18.029 --> 00:18:22.501 line:0%
<i> DEVELOPING A TASTE FOR MEAT.</i>

00:18:29.774 --> 00:18:33.044 line:0%
<i> THE RAVEN'S A NOISY
 IRRITANT AND IT COULD ALERT</i>

00:18:33.144 --> 00:18:38.350 line:0%
<i> RIVAL PREDATORS
 TO THE KILL...</i>

00:18:40.919 --> 00:18:45.858 line:0%
<i> BUT SOMEONE'S
 LATE TO DINNER.</i>

00:18:55.934 --> 00:19:01.039
♪ ♪

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:08.147 line:0%
<i> KITTENS WILL BE KITTENS,
 NO MATTER HOW BIG.</i>

00:19:10.882 --> 00:19:13.551 line:0%
<i> OUTSIDE THE PARK,
 COUGARS ARE STILL SHOT BY</i>

00:19:13.651 --> 00:19:16.421 line:0%
<i> THOSE WHO THINK THEY'RE
 A THREAT TO LIVESTOCK.</i>

00:19:16.521 --> 00:19:22.161 line:0%
<i> BUT HERE THE
 LITTLE FAMILY IS SAFE.</i>

00:19:32.204 --> 00:19:35.406
♪ ♪

00:19:35.506 --> 00:19:37.942 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE'S PART OF
 THE ROCKIES USED TO BE</i>

00:19:38.042 --> 00:19:39.811 line:0%
<i> ON THE SEA FLOOR.</i>

00:19:39.911 --> 00:19:42.981 line:0%
<i> THE CLASH OF CONTINENTS
 HAS DRIVEN THEM 8,000 FEET</i>

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:48.220 line:0%
<i> INTO THE AIR.</i>

00:19:51.323 --> 00:19:54.193 line:0%
<i> BUT WHAT THE EARTH LIFTS,
 WATER SLICES,</i>

00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:56.895 line:0%
<i> REVEALING THE YELLOW
 ROCK CANYON THAT GIVES THE</i>

00:19:56.995 --> 00:20:00.699 line:0%
<i> PARK ITS NAME.</i>

00:20:00.799 --> 00:20:03.501 line:0%
<i> THE YELLOWSTONE RIVER,
 THE LIFEBLOOD OF THE PARK,</i>

00:20:03.601 --> 00:20:08.674 line:0%
<i> POURS INTO THE VALLEYS.</i>

00:20:13.177 --> 00:20:16.514 line:0%
<i> THE HERD MUST MOVE IN
 SEARCH OF BETTER GRAZING AND</i>

00:20:16.614 --> 00:20:20.986 line:0%
<i> OUR CALF IS
 READY TO JOIN THEM.</i>

00:20:28.359 --> 00:20:30.796 line:0%
<i> JUST HOURS AFTER HIS BIRTH,</i>

00:20:30.896 --> 00:20:33.298 line:0%
<i> THIS 40-POUND
 FELLA CAN KEEP UP WITH</i>

00:20:33.398 --> 00:20:36.968 line:0%
<i> HIS 1,000-POUND MOM.</i>

00:20:37.068 --> 00:20:38.770 line:0%
<i> HE'LL FOLLOW MOM ANYWHERE,</i>

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:44.476 line:0%
<i> EVEN IF IT MIGHT BE
 THE DEATH OF HIM.</i>

00:20:46.244 --> 00:20:51.416 line:0%
<i> OTHER CREATURES HAVE
 NOT BEEN SO LUCKY.</i>

00:20:51.516 --> 00:20:57.488 line:0%
<i> WOLVES NO LONGER HUNT, BUT
 SCAVENGE AT THEIR LEISURE.</i>

00:20:58.156 --> 00:21:04.730 line:0%
<i> NOT FAR AWAY, THE PACK FEASTS
 ON STILL ANOTHER FALLEN BISON.</i>

00:21:07.032 --> 00:21:11.102 line:0%
<i> BUT SOMEONE'S GOTTEN
 WIND OF THEIR BOUNTY.</i>

00:21:11.202 --> 00:21:14.606 line:0%
<i> A GRIZZLY MOTHER
 AND THREE BIG CUBS.</i>

00:21:14.706 --> 00:21:17.008 line:0%
<i> RAISING TRIPLETS
 IN YELLOWSTONE IS QUITE</i>

00:21:17.108 --> 00:21:20.445 line:0%
<i> THE ACCOMPLISHMENT.</i>

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.755 line:0%
<i> EVEN AMONG GRIZZLIES,</i>

00:21:30.855 --> 00:21:36.928 line:0%
<i> WHO ARE NOTORIOUSLY GOOD
 MOTHERS, SHE'S REMARKABLE.</i>

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:44.369 line:0%
<i> WITH SO MANY MOUTHS TO FEED,</i>

00:21:44.469 --> 00:21:48.940 line:0%
<i> SHE HAS LITTLE CHOICE
 BUT TO TAKE ON THE PACK.</i>

00:21:58.316 --> 00:22:02.921
♪ ♪

00:22:13.598 --> 00:22:15.500 line:0%
<i> JUST WHEN IT LOOKS AS
 THOUGH THERE'S ENOUGH</i>

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:17.402 line:0%
<i> TO GO AROUND...</i>

00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:20.104 line:0%
<i> SOMEONE ELSE
 IS ON THE SCENT.</i>

00:22:20.204 --> 00:22:24.208 line:0%
<i> A LONE MALE.</i>

00:22:24.308 --> 00:22:28.747 line:0%
<i> THIS IS BAD NEWS.</i>

00:22:30.314 --> 00:22:35.620 line:0%
<i> MALE GRIZZLIES
 SOMETIMES KILL CUBS.</i>

00:22:43.695 --> 00:22:47.632 line:0%
<i> TIME FOR HIM TO BACK OFF.</i>

00:22:59.444 --> 00:23:01.312 line:0%
<i> A MALE BEAR, A YOUNGSTER,</i>

00:23:01.412 --> 00:23:06.718 line:0%
<i> IS NO MATCH FOR A
 RILED-UP MAMA BEAR.</i>

00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:09.654 line:0%
<i> THESE WOLVES ARE
 CONTENT TO WAIT,</i>

00:23:09.755 --> 00:23:12.290 line:0%
<i> WATCH AND AMUSE
 THEMSELVES TILL THE BEARS</i>

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:17.396 line:0%
<i> HAVE HAD THEIR FILL.</i>

00:23:26.737 --> 00:23:30.141 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE IS THE ONLY
 PLACE IN THE US WHERE BISON</i>

00:23:30.241 --> 00:23:35.947 line:0%
<i> HAVE LIVED CONTINUOUSLY
 SINCE PREHISTORIC TIMES.</i>

00:23:38.583 --> 00:23:41.619 line:0%
<i> THEIR RELENTLESS SEARCH
 FOR BETTER GRAZING GROUNDS</i>

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:46.792 line:0%
<i> MEANS CROSSING RIVERS,
 LIKE THE LAMAR...</i>

00:23:57.769 --> 00:24:00.772 line:0%
<i> CROSSINGS ARE NO BIG
 DEAL FOR THE GROWN-UPS,</i>

00:24:00.872 --> 00:24:06.945 line:0%
<i> BUT A DAUNTING BUSINESS
 FOR OUR 7-DAY-OLD CALF.</i>

00:24:09.146 --> 00:24:14.919 line:0%
<i> RUSHING SNOWMELT MAKES
 THE LAMAR TREACHEROUS.</i>

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:21.026 line:0%
<i> OUR LITTLE GUY IS
 UNDERSTANDABLY DUBIOUS.</i>

00:24:31.836 --> 00:24:33.704 line:0%
<i> BUT WHEN MOTHER
 MAKES HER MOVE,</i>

00:24:33.804 --> 00:24:38.810 line:0%
<i> HE HAS NO CHOICE
 BUT TO FOLLOW.</i>

00:24:43.314 --> 00:24:47.551 line:0%
<i> AND ALMOST IMMEDIATELY
 THINGS START TO GO WRONG.</i>

00:24:47.652 --> 00:24:52.757 line:0%
<i> THE CURRENT IS JUST TOO MUCH.</i>

00:25:02.834 --> 00:25:07.305
♪ ♪

00:25:07.405 --> 00:25:10.342 line:0%
<i> HIS MOTHER TURNS BACK,
 TRYING TO KEEP HIM SAFELY</i>

00:25:10.442 --> 00:25:16.047 line:0%
<i> UPSTREAM OF HER.</i>

00:25:23.588 --> 00:25:25.757 line:0%
<i> BUT THE WATER IS TOO SWIFT...</i>

00:25:25.857 --> 00:25:29.794 line:0%
<i> AND HE IS TOO YOUNG.</i>

00:25:31.662 --> 00:25:34.232 line:0%
<i> SHE REALIZES HER MISTAKE...</i>

00:25:34.332 --> 00:25:36.100 line:0%
<i> TOO LATE.</i>

00:25:36.200 --> 00:25:38.636 line:0%
<i> HE'S AT THE
 MERCY OF THE RIVER.</i>

00:25:38.736 --> 00:25:42.173 line:0%
<i> WHAT HAPPENS NEXT
 WILL DEFY BELIEF.</i>

00:25:51.416 --> 00:25:54.352 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: A CALF SWEPT
 AWAY BY THE LAMAR SHOULD HAVE</i>

00:25:54.452 --> 00:25:58.056 line:0%
<i> NO CHANCE OF SURVIVAL.</i>

00:25:59.257 --> 00:26:02.960 line:0%
<i> BUT SOMETHING
 REMARKABLE HAS HAPPENED.</i>

00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:07.832 line:0%
<i> HE HAS WASHED UP ONTO
 A LITTLE GRAVEL ISLAND.</i>

00:26:15.005 --> 00:26:17.575 line:0%
<i> HE'S CHILLED AND
 UTTERLY SPENT...</i>

00:26:17.675 --> 00:26:21.846 line:0%
<i> AND MOTHER IS
 NOWHERE IN SIGHT.</i>

00:26:30.554 --> 00:26:33.524 line:0%
<i> AS THE COLD
 YELLOWSTONE NIGHT FALLS,</i>

00:26:33.624 --> 00:26:38.396 line:0%
<i> ALL SEEMS LOST...</i>

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:55.213
♪ ♪

00:27:00.851 --> 00:27:06.358 line:0%
<i> DAYBREAK REVEALS A WOLF
 ON A KILL IN THE RIVER.</i>

00:27:08.292 --> 00:27:14.065 line:0%
<i> BUT IT'S AN ELK,
 NOT OUR BISON CALF.</i>

00:27:18.369 --> 00:27:22.874 line:0%
<i> SOMEHOW, OUR LITTLE ONE
 HAS SURVIVED THE NIGHT.</i>

00:27:22.974 --> 00:27:27.746 line:0%
<i> BUT HE'S STILL STRANDED.</i>

00:27:32.349 --> 00:27:38.723 line:0%
<i> ANY HOPE OF RESCUE SEEMS TO
 BE MOVING ON WITH HIS HERD.</i>

00:27:39.824 --> 00:27:45.230 line:0%
<i> EVEN HIS MOTHER
 SEEMS TO HAVE GIVEN UP.</i>

00:27:52.570 --> 00:27:58.943 line:0%
<i> THE INSTINCT TO STAY WITH
 THE HERD IS OVERWHELMING.</i>

00:28:04.048 --> 00:28:08.219 line:0%
<i> AND THAT'S FOR
 A GOOD REASON...</i>

00:28:08.686 --> 00:28:11.188 line:0%
<i> PREDATORS ARE
 NEVER FAR AWAY;</i>

00:28:11.288 --> 00:28:14.692 line:0%
<i> SUCH AS COYOTES...</i>

00:28:14.792 --> 00:28:19.397 line:0%
<i> AND A LONE BLACK WOLF.</i>

00:28:28.606 --> 00:28:32.310 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:28:32.610 --> 00:28:34.945 line:0%
<i> BACK DOWNRIVER,
 AGAINST ALL ODDS,</i>

00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:37.982 line:0%
<i> THE BISON CALF IS HOLDING ON.</i>

00:28:38.082 --> 00:28:42.520 line:0%
<i> BUT HE SEEMS OUT OF OPTIONS.</i>

00:28:47.892 --> 00:28:51.529 line:0%
<i> AND JUST WHEN THINGS
 COULDN'T GET ANY WORSE...</i>

00:28:51.629 --> 00:28:54.732 line:0%
<i> THEY DO.</i>

00:28:54.932 --> 00:29:00.038 line:0%
<i> A STRAPPING YOUNG
 WOLF HAS SPOTTED HIM.</i>

00:29:00.838 --> 00:29:06.077 line:0%
<i> THIS TINY ISLAND
 OFFERS NO ESCAPE.</i>

00:29:11.983 --> 00:29:17.822 line:0%
<i> BUT APPARENTLY, OUR
 CALF IS NO ORDINARY CALF.</i>

00:29:18.723 --> 00:29:22.327 line:0%
<i> HOPELESSLY OUTMATCHED,
 WITH THE COURAGE OF INNOCENCE,</i>

00:29:22.427 --> 00:29:25.262 line:0%
<i> HE'S NOT GOING
 DOWN WITHOUT A FIGHT.</i>

00:29:25.362 --> 00:29:30.168 line:0%
<i> AND THE INEXPERIENCED
 WOLF FLAILS.</i>

00:29:39.277 --> 00:29:41.879
♪ ♪

00:29:41.979 --> 00:29:45.583 line:0%
<i> AND THEN, A NOISE.</i>

00:29:47.685 --> 00:29:51.555 line:0%
<i> AN IMPOSSIBLE,
 WONDERFUL NOISE.</i>

00:29:51.922 --> 00:29:53.958 line:0%
<i> HERE COMES THE CAVALRY.</i>

00:29:54.058 --> 00:29:55.994 line:0%
<i> BUT IS IT IN TIME?</i>

00:29:59.297 --> 00:30:01.933 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: WITH AN ADULT
 BISON CHARGING TO THE RESCUE,</i>

00:30:02.033 --> 00:30:06.838 line:0%
<i> OUR CALF NOW
 TURNS ON THE WOLF.</i>

00:30:14.846 --> 00:30:18.383
♪ ♪

00:30:18.483 --> 00:30:20.751 line:0%
<i> THE CALF SEEMS TO WONDER,</i>

00:30:20.851 --> 00:30:25.323 line:0%
<i> COULD THIS REALLY
 BE HIS MOTHER?</i>

00:30:31.028 --> 00:30:32.764 line:0%
<i> IT SURE IS.</i>

00:30:32.864 --> 00:30:38.870 line:0%
<i> AND THE WOLF CAN'T
 BELIEVE HIS EYES.</i>

00:30:40.338 --> 00:30:43.974 line:0%
<i> FAMISHED, THE PLUCKY
 LITTLE FIGHTER LOSES NO TIME</i>

00:30:44.074 --> 00:30:50.215 line:0%
<i> FILLING UP ON HIS
 MOTHER'S RICH MILK.</i>

00:30:57.388 --> 00:31:04.028 line:0%
<i> AND THIS WOLF HAS BEEN
 THOROUGHLY BUFFALOED!</i>

00:31:07.698 --> 00:31:13.438 line:0%
<i> IN YELLOWSTONE, SECOND
 CHANCES ARE HARD TO COME BY</i>

00:31:15.540 --> 00:31:20.078 line:0%
<i> AND IT'S GOOD TO BE ALIVE.</i>

00:31:29.687 --> 00:31:35.994
♪ ♪

00:31:47.672 --> 00:31:53.912
♪ ♪

00:32:00.284 --> 00:32:03.154 line:0%
<i> SPRING RUSHES INTO
 SUMMER AND THE PARK</i>

00:32:03.254 --> 00:32:08.526 line:0%
<i> SHOWS OFF ITS COLORS.</i>

00:32:12.329 --> 00:32:17.534 line:0%
<i> SUMMER IS A TRULY
 GLORIOUS TIME IN YELLOWSTONE.</i>

00:32:17.634 --> 00:32:19.837 line:0%
<i> AND A GREAT TIME
 TO BE A RIVER OTTER,</i>

00:32:19.938 --> 00:32:23.040 line:0%
<i> OR EVEN BETTER, A
 PAIR OF OTTER BROTHERS.</i>

00:32:23.140 --> 00:32:27.211 line:0%
<i> TO SEE THESE GUYS IN
 SUMMER IS A RARE TREAT.</i>

00:32:36.420 --> 00:32:39.257 line:0%
<i> RIGHT NOW, YUMMY
 YELLOWSTONE CUTTHROAT TROUT</i>

00:32:39.357 --> 00:32:44.629 line:0%
<i> ARE FIGHTING THEIR WAY
 UPSTREAM FROM LAKES TO SPAWN.</i>

00:32:50.267 --> 00:32:53.070 line:0%
<i> MORE THAN THREE MILLION
 YELLOWSTONE CUTTHROAT TROUT</i>

00:32:53.170 --> 00:32:55.105 line:0%
<i> USED TO PLY THESE WATERS.</i>

00:32:55.206 --> 00:32:57.407 line:0%
<i> BUT THE ILLEGAL
 INTRODUCTION OF LAKE TROUT</i>

00:32:57.508 --> 00:33:01.979 line:0%
<i> HAS DECIMATED THE POPULATION.</i>

00:33:02.079 --> 00:33:06.551 line:0%
<i> OTTERS LOVE FISH.</i>

00:33:07.217 --> 00:33:11.990 line:0%
<i> BROTHER HAS HIS LUNCH.</i>

00:33:13.157 --> 00:33:19.530 line:0%
<i> THE OTHER CAN'T
 QUITE REEL HIS IN.</i>

00:33:22.066 --> 00:33:26.738 line:0%
<i> THIS SHOULD BE
 LIKE FISH IN A BARREL.</i>

00:33:31.008 --> 00:33:35.680 line:0%
<i> FINALLY, SUCCESS!</i>

00:33:43.154 --> 00:33:45.422 line:0%
<i> BACK AT THE
 SODA BUTTE CONDOS,</i>

00:33:45.522 --> 00:33:50.495 line:0%
<i> INSISTENT MOUTHS
 GAPE AT EVERY DOOR.</i>

00:33:55.233 --> 00:33:57.368 line:0%
<i> THE CLIFF SWALLOW
 PARENTS FRANTICALLY FEED</i>

00:33:57.468 --> 00:33:59.436 line:0%
<i> THEIR INSATIABLE OFFSPRING,</i>

00:33:59.537 --> 00:34:04.375 line:0%
<i> WHO WILL FLY THE
 NEST IN JUST THREE WEEKS.</i>

00:34:11.882 --> 00:34:15.819 line:0%
<i> BUT SOMETIMES MOM AND
 DAD ARE SO ENTHUSIASTIC...</i>

00:34:15.919 --> 00:34:21.159 line:0%
<i> EVEN THESE CHICKS CAN
 GET A LITTLE UNGRATEFUL.</i>

00:34:30.168 --> 00:34:35.773 line:0%
<i> THE DAYS OF SUMMER
 PASS ALL TOO QUICKLY, HERE.</i>

00:34:45.616 --> 00:34:48.719 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE'S MAGNIFICENT
 LANDSCAPES ARE A</i>

00:34:48.819 --> 00:34:50.520 line:0%
<i> STUDY IN CONTRASTS.</i>

00:34:50.620 --> 00:34:52.956 line:0%
<i> THIS PART OF THE
 ROCKIES IS ANCIENT;</i>

00:34:53.056 --> 00:34:59.263 line:0%
<i> ABOUT 75 MILLION YEARS OLD.</i>

00:35:01.365 --> 00:35:05.102 line:0%
<i> BUT THE STEAMING PLAINS
 ARE CONSTANTLY BEING REBORN,</i>

00:35:05.202 --> 00:35:09.206 line:0%
<i> THANKS TO THE
 SUPER-VOLCANO SIMMERING BELOW.</i>

00:35:09.306 --> 00:35:12.009 line:0%
<i> HERE THE GUTS OF THE
 PLANET ARE PERILOUSLY CLOSE</i>

00:35:12.109 --> 00:35:15.546 line:0%
<i> TO THE SURFACE.</i>

00:35:18.515 --> 00:35:21.118 line:0%
<i> GURGLING MUDPOTS
 AND FUMAROLES,</i>

00:35:21.218 --> 00:35:23.654 line:0%
<i> LIKE THE RED SPOUTER IN
 THE FOUNTAIN PAINT POT,</i>

00:35:23.754 --> 00:35:28.792 line:0%
<i> GIVE THE BAREST HINTS
 OF THE POWER BENEATH.</i>

00:35:28.892 --> 00:35:32.763 line:0%
<i> BUT 640,000 YEARS AGO,
 IT BLEW UP WITH THE FORCE</i>

00:35:32.863 --> 00:35:37.235 line:0%
<i> OF A THOUSAND ATOMIC BOMBS.</i>

00:35:38.069 --> 00:35:41.105 line:0%
<i> AND THE GEYSERS REMIND
 US THAT IT FULLY INTENDS TO</i>

00:35:41.205 --> 00:35:43.874 line:0%
<i> BLOW UP AGAIN...</i>

00:35:43.974 --> 00:35:47.879 line:0%
<i> SOME SAY IT'S OVERDUE.</i>

00:35:51.882 --> 00:35:53.384 line:0%
<i> IT'S LATE SUMMER.</i>

00:35:53.484 --> 00:35:55.586 line:0%
<i> OUR CALF IS
 PACKING ON POUNDS.</i>

00:35:55.686 --> 00:36:00.391 line:0%
<i> HIS RED COAT
 IS TURNING BROWN.</i>

00:36:06.129 --> 00:36:12.270 line:0%
<i> THERE'S EVEN THE TINIEST HINT
 OF A HUMP GROWING ON HIS BACK.</i>

00:36:17.441 --> 00:36:21.946 line:0%
<i> IT'S A BITTERSWEET
 TIME FOR SOME.</i>

00:36:30.254 --> 00:36:33.523 line:0%
<i> OUR THREE GRIZZLY CUBS
 HAVE BEEN DRIVEN OFF BY</i>

00:36:33.623 --> 00:36:36.360 line:0%
<i> THEIR ONCE-ATTENTIVE
 MOTHER SO SHE CAN MATE AGAIN.</i>

00:36:36.460 --> 00:36:38.495 line:0%
<i> SHE DID HER JOB WELL,
 THOUGH...</i>

00:36:38.595 --> 00:36:43.768 line:0%
<i> THEY'RE FAT AND STRONG.</i>

00:36:53.443 --> 00:36:56.313 line:0%
<i> THE LAKE PROVIDES RELIEF
 FROM THE HEAT AND ADDS SOME</i>

00:36:56.413 --> 00:36:59.450 line:0%
<i> MUCH-NEEDED
 GREENS TO THEIR DIETS.</i>

00:36:59.550 --> 00:37:04.789 line:0%
<i> THEY FILL UP ON
 TASTY AQUATIC PLANTS.</i>

00:37:13.697 --> 00:37:19.870
♪ ♪

00:37:21.105 --> 00:37:24.575 line:0%
<i> WATER FIGHTS ARE GOOD FUN,
 AND GENTLE PRACTICE FOR</i>

00:37:24.675 --> 00:37:29.647 line:0%
<i> SETTLING SCORES LATER ON.</i>

00:37:35.085 --> 00:37:37.854 line:0%
<i> THE TRIPLETS WILL SOON
 GO THEIR SEPARATE WAYS,</i>

00:37:37.954 --> 00:37:43.060 line:0%
<i> TO FACE THEIR
 FIRST WINTER ALONE.</i>

00:37:54.305 --> 00:37:57.007 line:0%
<i> AT THE LARGEST THERMAL
 FEATURE IN THE PARK,</i>

00:37:57.107 --> 00:37:58.743 line:0%
<i> THINGS ARE HEATING UP.</i>

00:37:58.843 --> 00:38:01.645 line:0%
<i> THE GRAND PRISMATIC SPRING
 GETS ITS VIVID COLORS FROM</i>

00:38:01.745 --> 00:38:06.817 line:0%
<i> A RAINBOW OF
 HEAT-LOVING BACTERIA.</i>

00:38:08.953 --> 00:38:14.124 line:0%
<i> AND THE PLAINS NEARBY ARE
 ABOUT TO HOST A SPECTACLE.</i>

00:38:14.224 --> 00:38:15.926 line:0%
<i> THE BULLS ARE GATHERING.</i>

00:38:16.026 --> 00:38:18.428 line:0%
<i> SOON THE FLATS WILL
 REVERBERATE WITH THE THUNDER</i>

00:38:18.529 --> 00:38:22.633 line:0%
<i> OF HOOVES AND THE
 CRACK OF MIGHTY SKULLS.</i>

00:38:22.733 --> 00:38:26.570 line:0%
<i> THE RUT IS ABOUT TO BEGIN.</i>

00:38:34.544 --> 00:38:38.415 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: THE BISON RUT
 IS SHEER PANDEMONIUM.</i>

00:38:38.515 --> 00:38:41.718 line:0%
<i> SNORTING AND SNUFFLING,
 BELLOWING AND BELCHING MEANS</i>

00:38:41.818 --> 00:38:46.356 line:0%
<i> THE AIR IS THICK
 WITH TESTOSTERONE.</i>

00:38:46.456 --> 00:38:48.826 line:0%
<i> THERE'S A GOOD DEAL OF
 COMPETITIVE WALLOWING...</i>

00:38:48.926 --> 00:38:51.829 line:0%
<i> BATHING IN DUST AND
 ROLLING IN THEIR OWN URINE</i>

00:38:51.929 --> 00:38:55.533 line:0%
<i> TO INTIMIDATE RIVALS.</i>

00:38:58.436 --> 00:39:03.641 line:0%
<i> NOW FOR THE DOGGED
 PURSUIT OF THE FEMALES.</i>

00:39:13.718 --> 00:39:18.622 line:0%
<i> EACH DAY BRINGS MORE
 BULLS TO THE VALLEY,</i>

00:39:22.125 --> 00:39:27.565 line:0%
<i> LURED BY THE SCENTS AND
 SOUNDS OF PROCREATION.</i>

00:39:31.001 --> 00:39:34.504 line:0%
<i> MATING IS A QUICK AND
 UNROMANTIC BUSINESS.</i>

00:39:34.604 --> 00:39:37.807 line:0%
<i> IF IT TAKES, SHE'LL
 CARRY THE BABY FOR NINE MONTHS</i>

00:39:37.907 --> 00:39:43.781 line:0%
<i> THROUGH THE
 MERCILESS WINTER AHEAD.</i>

00:39:49.352 --> 00:39:54.058 line:0%
<i> TANGY HORMONES
 DRIFT ON THE BREEZE.</i>

00:39:56.193 --> 00:39:59.396 line:0%
<i> THE BULL IS ALREADY
 CHECKING THE NEXT FEMALE:</i>

00:39:59.497 --> 00:40:03.501 line:0%
<i> HE SAVORS HER
 READINESS WITH A LIP-CURL.</i>

00:40:06.436 --> 00:40:08.972 line:0%
<i> BUT THERE'S
 TROUBLE ON THE HORIZON.</i>

00:40:09.072 --> 00:40:15.112 line:0%
<i> A ONE TON LIVING
 MOUNTAIN OF MUSCLE AND SKULL.</i>

00:40:23.487 --> 00:40:28.492 line:0%
<i> AND HE'S READY TO RUMBLE.</i>

00:40:35.499 --> 00:40:40.538 line:0%
<i> THE CHALLENGE
 MUST BE ANSWERED.</i>

00:40:48.411 --> 00:40:54.752 line:0%
<i> HIGH NOON IN THE
 YELLOWSTONE CORRAL.</i>

00:40:57.787 --> 00:40:59.723 line:0%
<i> THEIR MASSIVE
 HEADS AND NECKS ARE</i>

00:40:59.823 --> 00:41:04.962 line:0%
<i> BIOLOGICALLY ENGINEERED
 TO ABSORB ENORMOUS IMPACTS.</i>

00:41:15.172 --> 00:41:21.745
♪ ♪

00:41:31.588 --> 00:41:38.596
♪ ♪

00:41:45.702 --> 00:41:51.609 line:0%
<i> NOW THERE'S A
 NEW SHERIFF IN TOWN.</i>

00:42:01.451 --> 00:42:04.288 line:0%
<i> OUR CALF, A TOUGH
 LITTLE SURVIVOR,</i>

00:42:04.388 --> 00:42:08.191 line:0%
<i> IS BOUND TO TAKE HIS PLACE
 AMONGST THE BULLS ONE DAY.</i>

00:42:08.291 --> 00:42:13.898 line:0%
<i> HE'S ALREADY SHOWN ENOUGH
 COURAGE TO LAST A LIFETIME.</i>

00:42:21.271 --> 00:42:27.311 line:0%
<i> THE BISON RUT DRAWS TO
 ITS END IN EARLY AUTUMN.</i>

00:42:34.118 --> 00:42:36.119 line:0%
<i> BY LATE SEPTEMBER...</i>

00:42:36.219 --> 00:42:41.625 line:0%
<i> THE FALL SUN SETS
 THE TETONS BLAZING.</i>

00:42:51.602 --> 00:42:56.639
♪ ♪

00:42:56.740 --> 00:43:00.844 line:0%
<i> WHILE THE MOOSE
 FATTEN UP FOR THE WINTER,</i>

00:43:00.944 --> 00:43:06.183 line:0%
<i> THE ELK ANNOUNCE
 THEIR OWN RUT HAS COME.</i>

00:43:16.493 --> 00:43:18.695 line:0%
<i> THEN, THE PLACE
 FALLS SILENT;</i>

00:43:18.795 --> 00:43:21.765 line:0%
<i> THE BISON ENJOY A LAST
 FEW MOMENTS OF PEACE BEFORE</i>

00:43:21.865 --> 00:43:27.137 line:0%
<i> THE ONSLAUGHT OF WINTER.</i>

00:43:33.744 --> 00:43:39.717 line:0%
<i> NOW ONLY THE VOLCANO
 BELOW MAKES ITSELF HEARD.</i>

00:43:43.420 --> 00:43:50.194 line:0%
<i> A REMINDER OF THE ENGINE THAT
 POWERS AND PROTECTS THIS PLACE</i>

00:43:50.294 --> 00:43:56.066 line:0%
<i> AND THE MAGNIFICENT
 CREATURES WE ALMOST LOST.</i>

00:43:57.767 --> 00:44:02.739 line:0%
<i> IN AMERICA'S
 OLDEST NATIONAL PARK.</i>

00:44:02.839 --> 00:44:05.809 line:0%
<i> YELLOWSTONE.</i>

